IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore): ss 5, 5A, 5B and 6 -- subsidiary, holding company, ultimate holding company,
-- wholly owned subsidiary, related corporations.
--
-- HOW A GROUP IS MODELLED. A group is a LIST OF DIRECT CONTROL LINKS: one link says that a parent corporation satisfies
-- s 5(1)(a) in respect of a subsidiary corporation (it controls the composition of its board, or more than half of its
-- voting power). s 5(1)(b) then makes "subsidiary" run up a chain of links, which the functions below follow, with a
-- bound (the number of links) so that a cyclic list ends. The list is taken as COMPLETE: a link not in it does not exist,
-- which is what lets s 5A(b), "not itself a subsidiary of any corporation", be decided. A part that has only the answer
-- "C is a subsidiary of P" as a fact does not need this module: it asks the input
-- `the corporation is a subsidiary of the other corporation` (PLAN section 7).
-- The earlier pass modelled groups the same way (a list of control links) with the s 5(3) counting rules carried on
-- each holding; this module does the same and says in NOTES.md where it reads differently.
--
-- The direct link itself is decided from the facts of s 5(2) (the directors) and s 5(3) (the holdings).

§ `Types`

-- One direct link: the parent controls the subsidiary under s 5(1)(a).
DECLARE `s 5(1) control link` HAS
    `the parent` IS A Corporation
    `the subsidiary` IS A Corporation

-- A director of the corporation whose board is in question, with the facts s 5(2) and s 5(3)(a) ask about him or her.
DECLARE `s 5(2) director` HAS
    `the other corporation can appoint or remove the director by the exercise of some power exercisable by it (as s 5(3) counts a power) without the consent or concurrence of any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the director cannot be appointed without the exercise in his or her favour by the other corporation of such a power` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the director's appointment follows necessarily from his or her being a director or other officer of the other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other corporation exercises that power only in a fiduciary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Who holds a block of voting power, in the terms s 5(3)(a) to (d) use.
DECLARE `s 5(3) who holds the shares or exercises the power` IS ONE OF
    `s 5(3) the other corporation itself`
    `s 5(3) a nominee for the other corporation`
    `s 5(3) a subsidiary of the other corporation`
    `s 5(3) a nominee for a subsidiary of the other corporation`
    `s 5(3) any other person`

-- A block of shares or power, with the facts s 5(3) turns on.
DECLARE `s 5(3) holding` HAS
    `who holds it` IS A `s 5(3) who holds the shares or exercises the power`
    `the votes it carries` IS A NUMBER
    `it is held in a fiduciary capacity, the corporation it is held for being concerned only in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is held by virtue of the provisions of debentures of the firstmentioned corporation or of a trust deed securing an issue of them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ordinary business of the corporation it is held for, or of its subsidiary holding it, includes the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is held by way of security only for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of that business` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The kinds of member s 5B lists.
DECLARE `s 5B kind of member` IS ONE OF
    `s 5B the other corporation`
    `s 5B a nominee of the other corporation`
    `s 5B a subsidiary of the other corporation`
    `s 5B a nominee of a subsidiary of the other corporation`
    `s 5B any other person`

-- A member of the firstmentioned corporation, and (for a subsidiary, or a nominee of one) the kinds of its own members.
DECLARE `s 5B member` HAS
    `what the member is` IS A `s 5B kind of member`
    `the kinds of member of that subsidiary` IS A LIST OF `s 5B kind of member`

§ `Section 5(2): the composition of the board`

-- src:2007 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the composition of a
-- src:2008 | corporation’s board of directors is deemed to be controlled by another
-- src:2009 | corporation if that other corporation by the exercise of some power
-- src:2010 | exercisable by it without the consent or concurrence of any other
-- src:2011 | person can appoint or remove all or a majority of the directors, and for
-- src:2012 | the purposes of this provision that other corporation is deemed to
-- src:2013 | have power to make such an appointment if —
-- src:2015 | (a) a person cannot be appointed as a director without the
-- src:2016 | exercise in his or her favour by that other corporation of
-- src:2017 | such a power; or
-- src:2019 | (b) a person’s appointment as a director follows necessarily
-- src:2020 | from his or her being a director or other officer of that other
-- src:2021 | corporation.
@ref s 5(2) (src:2007-2021)
GIVEN director IS A `s 5(2) director`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(2) the other corporation has, or is deemed to have, power to appoint the director` MEANS
        (NOT director's `the other corporation exercises that power only in a fiduciary capacity`)
    AND (   director's `the other corporation can appoint or remove the director by the exercise of some power exercisable by it (as s 5(3) counts a power) without the consent or concurrence of any other person`
         OR director's `the director cannot be appointed without the exercise in his or her favour by the other corporation of such a power`
         OR director's `the director's appointment follows necessarily from his or her being a director or other officer of the other corporation`)

-- "can appoint or remove all or a majority of the directors": more than half of the directors. The text speaks of the
-- directors as a body ("all or a majority") and the deeming limbs (a) and (b) of "a person"; this module reads (a) and (b)
-- person by person and counts the directors the other corporation has power over (a reading, in NOTES.md).
@ref s 5(2) (src:2007-2021)
GIVEN directors IS A LIST OF `s 5(2) director`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(2) the other corporation controls the composition of the board` MEANS
    IF (count (filter (GIVEN d YIELD `s 5(2) the other corporation has, or is deemed to have, power to appoint the director` d) directors)) TIMES 2
       GREATER THAN count directors
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to be controlled by another corporation if that other corporation ... can appoint or remove all or a majority of the directors" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

§ `Section 5(3): the shares and the power that count`

-- src:2023 | (3) In determining whether one corporation is a subsidiary of
-- src:2024 | another corporation —
-- src:2026 | (a) any shares held or power exercisable by that other
-- src:2027 | corporation in a fiduciary capacity is to be treated as not
-- src:2028 | held or exercisable by it;
-- src:2030 | (b) subject to paragraphs (c) and (d), any shares held or power
-- src:2031 | exercisable —
-- src:2033 | (i) by any person as a nominee for that other corporation
-- src:2034 | (except where that other corporation is concerned
-- src:2035 | only in a fiduciary capacity); or
-- src:2037 | (ii) by, or by a nominee for, a subsidiary of that other
-- src:2038 | corporation, not being a subsidiary which is
-- src:2039 | concerned only in a fiduciary capacity,
-- src:2044 | (b) is to be treated as held or exercisable by that other
-- src:2045 | corporation;
-- src:2047 | (c) any shares held or power exercisable by any person by
-- src:2048 | virtue of the provisions of any debentures of the
-- src:2049 | firstmentioned corporation or of a trust deed for securing
-- src:2050 | any issue of such debentures is to be disregarded; and
-- src:2052 | (d) any shares held or power exercisable by, or by a nominee
-- src:2053 | for, that other corporation or its subsidiary (not being held
-- src:2054 | or exercisable as mentioned in paragraph (c)) is to be
-- src:2055 | treated as not held or exercisable by that other corporation
-- src:2056 | if the ordinary business of that other corporation or its
-- src:2057 | subsidiary (as the case may be) includes the lending of
-- src:2058 | money and the shares are held or power is exercisable as
-- src:2059 | aforesaid by way of security only for the purposes of a
-- src:2060 | transaction entered into in the ordinary course of that
-- src:2061 | business.
@ref s 5(3) (src:2023-2061)
GIVEN holding IS A `s 5(3) holding`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 5(3) the votes counted as held or exercisable by the other corporation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF holding's `it is held by virtue of the provisions of debentures of the firstmentioned corporation or of a trust deed securing an issue of them`
        THEN 0    -- (c): "is to be disregarded"
        IF holding's `who holds it` EQUALS `s 5(3) any other person`
        THEN 0    -- no limb of s 5(3) makes a stranger's holding the other corporation's
        IF    holding's `the ordinary business of the corporation it is held for, or of its subsidiary holding it, includes the lending of money`
          AND holding's `it is held by way of security only for a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of that business`
        THEN 0    -- (d): "treated as not held or exercisable by that other corporation"
        IF holding's `it is held in a fiduciary capacity, the corporation it is held for being concerned only in that capacity`
        THEN 0    -- (a): held in a fiduciary capacity is "treated as not held"; the exceptions in (b)(i) and (b)(ii) say the same of a nominee and of a subsidiary concerned only in that capacity
        OTHERWISE holding's `the votes it carries`    -- (a), (b)(i), (b)(ii): held by the corporation, by its nominee, or by (a nominee for) a subsidiary: "treated as held or exercisable by that other corporation"

-- The total counted for the other corporation.
@ref s 5(3) (src:2023-2061)
GIVEN holdings IS A LIST OF `s 5(3) holding`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 5(3) the total votes counted as held or exercisable by the other corporation` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN h YIELD `s 5(3) the votes counted as held or exercisable by the other corporation` h) holdings)

§ `Section 5(1): subsidiary`

-- The voting-power limb of s 5(1)(a): "controls more than half of the voting power of the firstmentioned corporation",
-- the votes counted as s 5(3) directs, against the firstmentioned corporation's total votes (a supplied number).
-- src:1988 | 5.—(1) For the purposes of this Act, a corporation is, subject to
-- src:1989 | subsection (3), deemed to be a subsidiary of another corporation, if —
-- src:1994 | (a) that other corporation —
-- src:1996 | (i) controls the composition of the board of directors of
-- src:1997 | the firstmentioned corporation; or
-- src:1999 | (ii) controls more than half of the voting power of the
-- src:2000 | firstmentioned corporation; or
-- src:2002 | (b) the firstmentioned corporation is a subsidiary of any
-- src:2003 | corporation which is that other corporation’s subsidiary.
@ref s 5(1) (src:1988-2003)
GIVEN holdings IS A LIST OF `s 5(3) holding`
      `the total votes of the firstmentioned corporation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(1)(a)(ii) the other corporation controls more than half of the voting power` MEANS
    IF (`s 5(3) the total votes counted as held or exercisable by the other corporation` holdings) TIMES 2
       GREATER THAN `the total votes of the firstmentioned corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "deemed to be a subsidiary of another corporation, if ... (ii) controls more than half of the voting power" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- s 5(1): the three limbs, as facts. (a)(i) and (a)(ii) are decided by the two functions above, or stated.
@ref s 5(1) (src:1988-2003)
GIVEN `the other corporation controls the composition of the board of the firstmentioned corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other corporation controls more than half of the voting power of the firstmentioned corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the firstmentioned corporation is a subsidiary of a corporation which is the other corporation's subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(1) the corporation is deemed to be a subsidiary of the other corporation` MEANS
    IF    `the other corporation controls the composition of the board of the firstmentioned corporation`
       OR `the other corporation controls more than half of the voting power of the firstmentioned corporation`
       OR `the firstmentioned corporation is a subsidiary of a corporation which is the other corporation's subsidiary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a corporation is, subject to subsection (3), deemed to be a subsidiary of another corporation, if" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- Following the links up a chain: the names of the corporations controlled, directly or through others, by those in the first list.
GIVEN links IS A LIST OF `s 5(1) control link`
      `the names reached so far` IS A LIST OF STRING
      `the steps still allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 5(1)(b) the names of the corporations controlled through` MEANS
    IF `the steps still allowed` AT MOST 0
    THEN `the names reached so far`
    ELSE `s 5(1)(b) the names of the corporations controlled through` links
            (nub (append `the names reached so far`
                    (map (GIVEN l YIELD l's `the subsidiary`'s `the name of the corporation`)
                         (filter (GIVEN l YIELD elem (l's `the parent`'s `the name of the corporation`) `the names reached so far`) links))))
            (`the steps still allowed` MINUS 1)

-- The subsidiaries of a corporation, direct or by a chain (s 5(1)(a) then (b)). The corporation itself is not one.
@ref s 5(1)(b) (src:2002-2003)
GIVEN links IS A LIST OF `s 5(1) control link`
      parent IS A Corporation
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 5(1) the names of the subsidiaries of` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN n YIELD NOT (n EQUALS parent's `the name of the corporation`))
        (`s 5(1)(b) the names of the corporations controlled through` links (LIST parent's `the name of the corporation`) (count links))

-- "Under section 5, is corporation C a subsidiary of corporation P?" from a list of direct links.
@ref s 5(1) (src:1988-2003)
GIVEN links IS A LIST OF `s 5(1) control link`
      subsidiary IS A Corporation
      parent IS A Corporation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(1) the corporation is a subsidiary of the other corporation, by the links` MEANS
    IF elem (subsidiary's `the name of the corporation`) (`s 5(1) the names of the subsidiaries of` links parent)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "deemed to be a subsidiary of another corporation, if" -- no chain of the listed links runs from the other corporation to this one (a failed "if", marginal reading (a); the list of links is taken as complete)

§ `Section 5(4) and (5): holding company`

-- src:2063 | (4) A reference in this Act to the holding company of a company or
-- src:2064 | other corporation is a reference to a corporation of which that last
-- src:2065 | mentioned company or corporation is a subsidiary.
@ref s 5(4) (src:2063-2065)
GIVEN links IS A LIST OF `s 5(1) control link`
      `the corporation` IS A Corporation
      `the other corporation` IS A Corporation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(4) the corporation is the holding company of the other corporation, by the links` MEANS
    IF elem (`the other corporation`'s `the name of the corporation`) (`s 5(1) the names of the subsidiaries of` links `the corporation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference ... to the holding company of a company or other corporation is a reference to a corporation of which that last mentioned company or corporation is a subsidiary"

-- s 5(5): the Depository.
-- src:2067 | (5) For the purposes of this Act, the Depository is not to be regarded
-- src:2068 | as a holding company of a corporation by reason only of the shares it
-- src:2069 | holds in that corporation as a bare trustee.
@ref s 5(5) (src:2067-2069)
GIVEN `the corporation is the Depository` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its only ground for being a holding company is shares it holds as a bare trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(5) the corporation is to be regarded as a holding company` MEANS
    IF `the corporation is the Depository` AND `its only ground for being a holding company is shares it holds as a bare trustee`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Depository is not to be regarded as a holding company of a corporation by reason only of the shares it holds in that corporation as a bare trustee"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says nothing of any other corporation, or of the Depository on another ground

§ `Section 5A: ultimate holding company`

-- src:2075 | 5A. For the purposes of this Act, a corporation is the ultimate
-- src:2076 | holding company of another corporation if —
-- src:2078 | (a) the other corporation is a subsidiary of the firstmentioned
-- src:2079 | corporation; and
-- src:2081 | (b) the firstmentioned corporation is not itself a subsidiary of
-- src:2082 | any corporation.
@ref s 5A (src:2075-2082)
GIVEN links IS A LIST OF `s 5(1) control link`
      `the corporation` IS A Corporation
      `the other corporation` IS A Corporation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5A the corporation is the ultimate holding company of the other corporation, by the links` MEANS
    IF    elem (`the other corporation`'s `the name of the corporation`) (`s 5(1) the names of the subsidiaries of` links `the corporation`)
       AND (NOT (any (GIVEN l YIELD l's `the subsidiary`'s `the name of the corporation` EQUALS `the corporation`'s `the name of the corporation`) links))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a corporation is the ultimate holding company of another corporation if (a) the other corporation is a subsidiary of the firstmentioned corporation; and (b) the firstmentioned corporation is not itself a subsidiary of any corporation" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a); the list of links is taken as complete)

-- The same, with the two limbs as facts.
@ref s 5A (src:2075-2082)
GIVEN `the other corporation is a subsidiary of the firstmentioned corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the firstmentioned corporation is itself a subsidiary of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5A the firstmentioned corporation is the ultimate holding company of the other corporation` MEANS
    IF `the other corporation is a subsidiary of the firstmentioned corporation` AND (NOT `the firstmentioned corporation is itself a subsidiary of a corporation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is the ultimate holding company of another corporation if (a) ... and (b) ..." (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

§ `Section 5B: wholly owned subsidiary`

-- A member is within paragraphs (a) to (d) when it is the other corporation, its nominee, a subsidiary of it none of whose
-- members is a person other than the other corporation or its nominee, or a nominee of such a subsidiary.
-- src:2086 | 5B. For the purposes of this Act, a corporation is a wholly owned
-- src:2087 | subsidiary of another corporation if none of the members of the
-- src:2088 | firstmentioned corporation is a person other than —
-- src:2093 | (a) that other corporation;
-- src:2095 | (b) a nominee of that other corporation;
-- src:2097 | (c) a subsidiary of that other corporation being a subsidiary
-- src:2098 | none of the members of which is a person other than that
-- src:2099 | other corporation or a nominee of that other corporation; or
-- src:2101 | (d) a nominee of such subsidiary.
@ref s 5B (src:2086-2101)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 5B kind of member`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5B the member of a subsidiary is the other corporation or its nominee` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 5B the other corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 5B a nominee of the other corporation` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref s 5B (src:2086-2101)
GIVEN member IS A `s 5B member`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5B the member is within paragraphs (a) to (d)` MEANS
    CONSIDER member's `what the member is`
    WHEN `s 5B the other corporation` THEN TRUE                                  -- (a)
    WHEN `s 5B a nominee of the other corporation` THEN TRUE                     -- (b)
    WHEN `s 5B a subsidiary of the other corporation` THEN                       -- (c)
        all (GIVEN k YIELD `s 5B the member of a subsidiary is the other corporation or its nominee` k) (member's `the kinds of member of that subsidiary`)
    WHEN `s 5B a nominee of a subsidiary of the other corporation` THEN          -- (d): a nominee of "such subsidiary", the (c) kind
        all (GIVEN k YIELD `s 5B the member of a subsidiary is the other corporation or its nominee` k) (member's `the kinds of member of that subsidiary`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref s 5B (src:2086-2101)
GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `s 5B member`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5B the corporation is a wholly owned subsidiary of the other corporation` MEANS
    IF all (GIVEN m YIELD `s 5B the member is within paragraphs (a) to (d)` m) members
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a corporation is a wholly owned subsidiary of another corporation if none of the members of the firstmentioned corporation is a person other than ..." (a failed "if"; the list of persons is closed by "none ... other than", marginal reading (a))

§ `Section 6: related corporations`

-- (a) the corporation is the holding company of the other; (b) it is a subsidiary of the other; (c) it is a subsidiary of the
-- holding company of the other, that is, both are subsidiaries of one corporation.
-- src:2104 | 6. Where a corporation —
-- src:2105 | (a) is the holding company of another corporation;
-- src:2106 | (b) is a subsidiary of another corporation; or
-- src:2107 | (c) is a subsidiary of the holding company of another
-- src:2108 | corporation,
-- src:2110 | that firstmentioned corporation and that other corporation are for the
-- src:2111 | purposes of this Act deemed to be related to each other.
@ref s 6 (src:2104-2111)
GIVEN links IS A LIST OF `s 5(1) control link`
      `the corporation` IS A Corporation
      `the other corporation` IS A Corporation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 the corporation and the other corporation are deemed to be related, by the links` MEANS
    IF    `s 5(4) the corporation is the holding company of the other corporation, by the links` links `the corporation` `the other corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `s 5(1) the corporation is a subsidiary of the other corporation, by the links` links `the corporation` `the other corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR any (GIVEN holding YIELD
                    (elem (`the corporation`'s `the name of the corporation`) (`s 5(1) the names of the subsidiaries of` links holding))
                AND (elem (`the other corporation`'s `the name of the corporation`) (`s 5(1) the names of the subsidiaries of` links holding)))
              (map (GIVEN l YIELD l's `the parent`) links)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a corporation (a) is the holding company of another corporation; (b) is a subsidiary of another corporation; or (c) is a subsidiary of the holding company of another corporation, ... deemed to be related" (a failed "where", the periods ruling (b)); and s 4(1) "related corporation" means a corporation deemed related "by virtue of section 6"

-- The three limbs as facts.
@ref s 6 (src:2104-2111)
GIVEN `the corporation is the holding company of the other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is a subsidiary of the other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is a subsidiary of the holding company of the other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 the corporations are deemed to be related to each other` MEANS
    IF    `the corporation is the holding company of the other corporation`
       OR `the corporation is a subsidiary of the other corporation`
       OR `the corporation is a subsidiary of the holding company of the other corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a corporation (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..., that firstmentioned corporation and that other corporation are for the purposes of this Act deemed to be related to each other" (a failed "where", the periods ruling (b))

§ `Section 4(1): "related corporation"`

-- "Related corporation" is the s 6 relation, named from the point of view of the firstmentioned corporation.
-- src:1694 | “related corporation”, in relation to a corporation, means a
-- src:1695 | corporation that is deemed to be related to the firstmentioned
-- src:1696 | corporation by virtue of section 6;
@ref s 4(1) "related corporation" (src:1694-1696)
GIVEN links IS A LIST OF `s 5(1) control link`
      `the corporation` IS A Corporation
      `the other corporation` IS A Corporation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "related corporation" the other corporation is a related corporation of the corporation, by the links` MEANS
    IF `s 6 the corporation and the other corporation are deemed to be related, by the links` links `the corporation` `the other corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'related corporation', in relation to a corporation, means a corporation that is deemed to be related to the firstmentioned corporation by virtue of section 6" (a "means" definition: a corporation not so deemed is not one)

@ref s 4(1) "related corporation" (src:1694-1696)
GIVEN `the other corporation is deemed to be related to the corporation by virtue of section 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) "related corporation" the other corporation is a related corporation of the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the other corporation is deemed to be related to the corporation by virtue of section 6`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a corporation that is deemed to be related to the firstmentioned corporation by virtue of section 6" (a "means" definition)
